## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical use of SageMaker multi-model endpoints, per-tenant routing, and controlled releases under data privacy constraints (PrivateLink). It blends model choice, infrastructure sizing, and a measurable validation plan suitable for entry-level engineers.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model endpoints and Model Registry
- Tenant-aware routing with API Gateway + Lambda
- PrivateLink data isolation and VPC considerations
- Canary rollouts and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for tenant routing to a variant
function routeTenant(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const variant = registry.getVariant(tenant);
  return endpoint.invoke({Body: req.body, Variant: variant});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test tenant isolation in practice?
- How would you monitor per-tenant drift and trigger rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates ability to design private, language-aware ML inference at scale with strict data locality and per-tenant isolation. Tests routing logic, canary deployment strategies, and cross-language drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model vs. per-language endpoints
- PrivateLink data residency and IAM isolation
- Canary rollouts and per-language versioning
- Model Registry + Pipelines for safe promotions
- Tenant-scoped storage and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Language route resolver
function routeEndpoint(lang) {
  const map = {
    en: 'ep-en',
    fr: 'ep-fr',
    de: 'ep-de'
  };
  return map[lang] || 'ep-default';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in deploying real-time ML systems within AWS for privacy-sensitive, multi-tenant environments requiring comprehensive monitoring, explainability, and rapid recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS PrivateLink and SageMaker endpoint architecture
- Private data lake integration with strict multi-tenant isolation
- Real-time drift detection and SHAP/IG explainability frameworks
- Provisioned concurrency and autoscaling for performance targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Explainer integration for inference transparency
function explainInference(model, input, featureNames) {
  const shapValues = model.predictSHAP(input);
  const igValues = model.predictIntegratedGradients(input);
  return {
    prediction: model.predict(input),
    explanations: {
      shap: shapValues,
      integratedGradients: igValues,
      featureNames: featureNames
    },
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    tenantId: extractTenantId(input)
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cost-aware, low-latency multi-model inference with per-language isolation, explainability, and secure data access via PrivateLink. It also probes rollout discipline and drift monitoring in production.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-model SageMaker endpoints with per-language routing
- SageMaker Clarify for real-time feature attributions
- PrivateLink access to private data lake and data residency
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring for safe production
- Caching for explanations to reduce latency impact

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo-CDK snippet outline for endpoint + Clarify integration
const clarifiyConfig = {
  enableExplainability: true,
  caching: true,
};
const endpoint = new sagemaker.CfnEndpoint(this, 'LangEndpoint', {
  // model shard per language
  endpointConfigName: 'LangMultiModelConfig',
  // integration with Clarify
